{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'L1|L8|400%|gpu|Safari|Firefox|late font|200 ms|2.5' packages/axylo/test packages/react/test docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md\n cat packages/react/test/types.check.tsx\"","aggregated_output":"docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:5:This plan builds the product defined in [02-product-spec.md](02-product-spec.md). Criterion IDs (F1, L1, A2, DX4, P1 …) refer to that spec; finding IDs (R5, D2 …) refer to [01-landscape.md](01-landscape.md).\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:186:| layout | Plot rectangle, tick sets, label boxes, legend and control placement | Implements L1, L3, L8. Takes a text-measurement interface as input. |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:214:**No animation system.** First render is not animated (I5). Updates cut, or tween for at most 200 ms where the cost is negligible, and not at all under reduced motion.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:239:### 2.5 Repository\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:251:Tooling: TypeScript strict; ESM output with `.d.ts`, plus IIFE files for `<script>` use; Vitest; fast-check for property tests; Playwright on Chromium, Firefox and WebKit; axe-core; size-limit on the packed distribution; API Extractor so that public API changes fail CI until reviewed; Changesets.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:253:CI runs on Linux, Windows and macOS. Windows runs the browser suite natively on Chromium, Firefox and Edge. Playwright's WebKit build stands in for Safari in CI; real Safari on macOS and iOS is a manual release check, named separately in results.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:298:- Title, `labelledBy`, subtitle, axis titles; toolbar with legend toggles; full tooltip and fixed readout (I1); label fitting (L1) and the too-small fallback (L8); states (L7); reference lines and bands.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:302:- L1's property test in three engines, including text-spacing overrides and a late-loading font, on a category-axis line chart with long labels.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:327:- `bars` fixture: starts at zero, long label handled by L1's remedies, missing bar distinct from zero.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:363:- Real Safari on macOS and iOS checked by hand.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:375:| Property | fast-check | Invariants that must hold for any data: F1, F2, F5, F7, F11, L1. |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:391:| DOM text costs too much with many charts on a page. | P5 is measured in M1. A fallback to canvas-drawn tick labels would give up user text spacing and forced-colors adaptation for those labels, so it must pass the same L1 and A6 tests before it is allowed. |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:394:| Layout promises collide in small tiles. | L8 defines the fallback; the property test covers down to 240 px. |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:395:| One person cannot hand-check real Safari, iOS, Android and Windows screen readers at every milestone. | Automated checks at every milestone; the manual rehearsal at M1, M4 and M8 only, recorded with dates and versions. Device access is a named dependency of those three milestones. |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:405:| Annotations beyond reference lines and bands | Text placement interacts with L1. |\npackages/axylo/test/theme/review.test.ts:19:    expect(check(theme('rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)', ['rgb(10, 10, 10)', 'rgb(255, 255, 255)']), 'rgb(0, 0, 0)')).toEqual([0]);\npackages/axylo/test/theme/review.test.ts:23:    expect(lowContrastSeries(theme('rgb(0, 0, 0)', ['rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1)', 'rgb(255, 255, 255)']))).toEqual([0]);\npackages/axylo/test/theme/color.test.ts:14:    expect(c('rgb(255, 0, 0)')).toEqual({ r: 1, g: 0, b: 0, a: 1 });\npackages/axylo/test/theme/color.test.ts:15:    expect(c('rgba(0, 0, 255, 0.5)')).toEqual({ r: 0, g: 0, b: 1, a: 0.5 });\npackages/axylo/test/theme/color.test.ts:17:    expect(c('rgb(0 128 0 / 25%)').g).toBeCloseTo(128 / 255, 9);\np