dware profiles | \"Desktop\": the reference machine, recorded with CPU, GPU, OS, display refresh rate and power settings. \"Throttled\": 4× CPU throttling through CDP, Chromium only. \"Phone\": one real mid-range Android phone, used at baseline calibration and at releases, when the device is available; when it is not, the result says so. |\n68:| Runnable combinations | Desktop × {Chrome, Firefox, WebKit}; Throttled × Chrome; Phone × Chrome. Nothing else is claimed. |\n122:| 9 | WebGL or WebGPU marks | Only if raster time is the measured bottleneck at sizes in the workload table. |\n146:| Before a release | Full set, plus Edge on Windows, Safari by hand, the phone profile when available, and all comparison libraries | Budgets P1–P7 and the previous release | A failed budget blocks the release, or the budget is changed in the spec with the measurements and a written reason. Never silently. |\n168:| Rendering to a pixel buffer or to WebGL/WebGPU from Rust | Only as a separate product decision | It replaces the renderer, brings its own text rendering, and does nothing for the DOM-based accessibility layer. |\n183:| Is the workload faster for the reader? | The lower bound of the 95% interval for the improvement in the workload's primary metric is at least 20%, and the absolute saving is at least the workload's declared minimum, in Chrome, Firefox and Safari or WebKit. A function-level microbenchmark is not evidence. |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
